       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum for adults:\n- **Immediate-release:** 2,550 mg/day, usually given as 850 mg three times daily.\n- **Extended-release:** 2,000 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day), or\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg twice daily, or\n- Another dose?\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you intend, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
